Removing your finger from 'z' will also stop it. This may have
something to do with the keyboard rate settings, but under both Linux
and MacOS X the behavior is such that immediately when I raise my
finger from 'z' it will stop. That is, no extra 'z's end in the
buffer.

My procedure for getting that last charge is that I position the wand
to 'z', look at the screen, press 'z' down, continue looking at the
screen, and keep 'z' pressed until I either get the charge or see a
monster move nearby at which point I lift my finger.



